# Chat Change Summary

This file summarizes the project changes made during this chat.

## Vercel Transfer / Screenshot Uploads

- Reworked desktop screenshot uploads so image bytes go directly from the agent to Vercel Blob instead of passing through the legacy `/api/screenshots` upload endpoint.
- Added a Blob client-upload token route:
  - `app/api/agent/screenshots/blob-upload/route.ts`
- Updated screenshot commit flow to save Vercel Blob URLs in the database:
  - `app/api/agent/screenshots/commit/route.ts`
- Disabled legacy screenshot file uploads through `/api/screenshots` by returning `410 Gone` for `POST /api/screenshots`.
- Updated screenshot deletion to delete the Blob object through `@vercel/blob`.
- Added `@vercel/blob` to the desktop agent package.

## Screenshot Compression

- Changed agent screenshot encoding from PNG/JPEG to WebP using `sharp`.
- Added adaptive compression targeting small screenshot sizes:
  - Target: about 55 KB per screenshot.
  - Server max upload size: 80 KB.
  - Candidate dimensions: `960x540`, `800x450`, `720x405`, `640x360`.
  - Candidate WebP qualities: `62`, `56`, `50`, `44`, `38`, `32`, `26`.
- Kept a JPEG fallback if WebP encoding fails at runtime.
- Added `sharp` to the desktop agent package.

## Supabase Migration / Env Handling

- Updated server-side Supabase env handling to support both older and newer Supabase env names:
  - `SUPABASE_URL`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`
  - `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`
  - `SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY`
  - `SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`
- Restored the agent Supabase Realtime policy-refresh connection after clarification.
- Updated the agent embedded config generator so new Supabase public URL/publishable key values can be embedded when the agent is rebuilt.
- The agent still refreshes security policy every five minutes through `/api/agent/policy-bundle`, and also listens for Supabase Realtime `policy-updated` broadcasts.

